# Maintainer: spmlinux contributors
#
# Runs Horizon's official (Windows) Spektrum Programmer under Wine.
# This is a stop gap while the native port (pkgname=spmlinux) is being
# finished: the GUI, model editors and firmware updates all work, but the
# FTDI D2XX layer needs a stand-in (see the package README).
#
# NOTE: the payload is Horizon Hobby / Mattel proprietary software and is
# packaged here only for local use.  Do not redistribute the built package.
pkgname=spektrum-programmer
pkgver=3.10.6.0
pkgrel=1
pkgdesc="Spektrum Programmer (Horizon Hobby) running under Wine on Linux"
arch=('x86_64')
url="https://spektrumrc.cachefly.net/apps/spektrum_programmer.html"
license=('custom: proprietary - Horizon Hobby, for local use only')
depends=('wine')
optdepends=(
    'libftd2xx: FTDI D2XX library needed by the wineftd2xx stand-in for the programming cable'
    'mingw-w64-gcc: build the ftd2xx.dll.so stand-in that bridges Wine to libftd2xx'
)
source=("spektrum-programmer-$pkgver.tar.gz")
sha256sums=('SKIP')
options=('!strip' '!debug')

package() {
    install -d "$pkgdir/opt/spektrum-programmer"
    cp -a "$srcdir/spektrum-programmer-$pkgver/." "$pkgdir/opt/spektrum-programmer/"

    install -d "$pkgdir/usr/bin"
    install -Dm755 /dev/stdin "$pkgdir/usr/bin/spektrum-programmer" <<'EOF'
#!/bin/sh
# Launch the (Windows) Spektrum Programmer under Wine.
#
# QT_OPENGL=software is required: with hardware OpenGL the 32-bit Qt5
# build dies with an unhandled exception (0xc0000409) during start-up.
set -e
APPDIR=/opt/spektrum-programmer
PREFIX="${SPM_WINE_PREFIX:-$HOME/.local/share/spektrum-programmer/wineprefix}"

if [ ! -d "$PREFIX" ]; then
    echo "Creating wine prefix in $PREFIX ..."
    WINEPREFIX="$PREFIX" wineboot -u >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
fi

exec env WINEPREFIX="$PREFIX" QT_OPENGL=software \
    wine "$APPDIR/SpmProgrammer.exe" "$@"
EOF

    install -d "$pkgdir/usr/share/applications"
    install -Dm644 /dev/stdin "$pkgdir/usr/share/applications/spektrum-programmer.desktop" <<'EOF'
[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Spektrum Programmer
Comment=Configure and update Spektrum receivers and transmitters
Exec=spektrum-programmer
Icon=spektrum-programmer
Terminal=false
Categories=Utility;Electronics;
EOF

    install -d "$pkgdir/usr/share/icons/hicolor/256x256/apps"
    install -Dm644 "$srcdir/spektrum-programmer-$pkgver/Images/Icon-Spektrum.ico" \
        "$pkgdir/usr/share/icons/hicolor/256x256/apps/spektrum-programmer.ico"

    install -Dm644 /dev/stdin "$pkgdir/usr/share/doc/$pkgname/README.md" <<'EOF'
# spektrum-programmer (Wine)

Horizon Hobby's Windows *Spektrum Programmer* 3.10.6.0 running under Wine.

    spektrum-programmer          # launch (creates a wine prefix on first run)

The GUI, the model editors, the account login and the firmware update all
work.  The launcher sets `QT_OPENGL=software`, because the 32-bit Qt5
build otherwise dies with an unhandled exception (0xc0000409) as soon as
it touches hardware OpenGL.

The **USB programming cable does not work out of the box**: the app talks
to the cable through FTDI's proprietary D2XX API (`ftd2xx.dll` +
`ftdibus.sys`), which Wine cannot provide.

## Making the cable work

1. Install the FTDI Linux D2XX library (or the open source libftd2xx).
2. Build the `wineftd2xx` stand-in (https://github.com/brentr/wineftd2xx):
   it provides `ftd2xx.dll.so` for Wine and forwards the D2XX calls to
   the Linux library.
3. Copy `ftd2xx.dll.so` over the copy in the wine prefix:
   `~/.local/share/spektrum-programmer/wineprefix/drive_c/windows/system32/`
4. Tell the stand-in which device to use and start the app with it:

       FTDID=0403:7C48 spektrum-programmer

   (`0403:7C48` is the Spektrum SPMA3065 cable; any FTDI device works.)

If you only want the model files and the protocol work, use the native
package `spmlinux` instead - no Wine, no driver.

This package contains proprietary Horizon Hobby software; it is meant for
local use only and must not be redistributed.
EOF
}
